WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.999 line:0
We play white and move first. Every piece is public.
Checkmate the opposing king to win.

00:00:06.999 --> 00:00:14.749 line:0
Select a piece, then a legal square. A knight
moves in an L and jumps over pieces.

00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:18.999 line:0
Black pushes a pawn. The move list uses
standard algebraic notation, such as Nc3.

00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:26.999 line:0
Fast-forward: knights and pawns come out and trade.
Pawns step forward but capture diagonally.

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:31.999 line:0
The black queen checks our king from e7.
In check, the next move must remove the threat.

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:35.999 line:0
We block with a bishop. You may also move
the king or capture the attacker.

00:00:35.999 --> 00:00:43.998 line:0
Fast-forward: a black knight captures with check
and our queen takes it. Black's king is driven away.

00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:54.748 line:0
Our pawn takes the rook on a8 and reaches the
last rank: it must promote. We pick the queen.

00:00:54.748 --> 00:01:01.998 line:0
A black bishop captures the new queen at once.

00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:09.999 line:0
Fast-forward: we castle, a knight checks, our queen
takes the blocker with check; black king to d8.

00:01:09.999 --> 00:01:14.999 line:0
Our queen moves to a8, checking again.

00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:17.999 line:0
The king cannot move away, capture the
attacker or block. This is checkmate.

00:01:17.999 --> 00:01:27.000 line:0
After 33 moves black is checkmated; white wins.
Stalemate, repetition and 50 quiet moves draw.
